# Giggora — build context exclusions.
#
# TWO REASONS THIS FILE EXISTS, and the second one matters more.
#
# 1. CORRECTNESS. Without it, `COPY explorer-web ./` copies the WINDOWS-built
#    node_modules over the Linux `npm ci` output inside the image. The build
#    then dies with
#      /app/node_modules/.bin/next: exec: line 33: node.exe: not found
#    because the .bin shims are Windows shims. Native modules are per-platform;
#    a host node_modules must never enter a Linux image.
#
# 2. SECRETS (brief §30). The build context is the repository ROOT, so without
#    these rules `blockchain/nodes/` — which holds the VALIDATOR PRIVATE KEYS —
#    and `.env` would be shipped into the build context and could land in an
#    image layer. Layers persist even if a later step deletes the file, and an
#    image gets pushed to registries. Do not remove these lines.

# ---- secrets: never in a build context ----
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
blockchain/nodes/
blockchain/keys/
blockchain/genesis/networkFiles/
**/key
**/key.pub
*.pem
secrets/
backups/

# ---- host-built dependencies: wrong platform ----
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/out
**/dist

# ---- chain data: large, regenerated, not needed to build ----
blockchain/data/
**/besu-data/

# ---- build/test artifacts ----
contracts/lib/
contracts/out/
contracts/cache/
contracts/broadcast/
coverage/
*.log

# ---- vcs and tooling ----
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
